  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Gusty winds from the northwest during the day \nFriday could lead to isolated power outages.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nCooler air moving in, with a strong pressure gradient, will lead\nto gusty winds over land during the day Friday. Anticipating max\ngusts 30-40 mph, with the greatest threat across Northern Maine\nand into the Bangor region. This will be strong enough to lead \nto isolated power outages. The primary threat is during the day \nFriday from mid-morning to sunset.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Potential for frost Saturday night across the \nnorth.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure will be building in Saturday evening from Canada. \nMovement of the high will determine how low temps can drop Saturday \nnight into Sunday morning. Operational guidance and ensemble members \nindicate that sfc high should be cresting over CWA around 06z Sunday \nwith return flow kicking in after this time. Winds should decouple \nand with uncertainty in thickness of cloud cover spilling into the \narea overnight have gone on the colder side of guidance with river \nvalleys dropping to near to just below freezing, mainly over nrn \nareas. Have included patchy frost in forecast for Saturday\nnight.",
